T* (- Chest tightness and nocturnal wheezing) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (HOSPITAL COURSE & TREATMENT SUMMARY:) Tj
T* (Patient presented with dyspnea and productive cough. Chest X-Ray on admission) Tj
T* (demonstrated bilateral peribronchial cuffing without focal consolidation or pleural effusion.) Tj
T* (He was treated with intravenous bronchodilators, short course IV Hydrocortisone,) Tj
T* (nebulization \(Levosalbutamol + Ipratropium\), and empirical antibiotic therapy) Tj
T* (\(Azithromycin 500mg IV OD for 3 days\). Glycemic levels were monitored and managed) Tj
T* (with regular insulin sliding scale during the acute steroid phase.) Tj
T* (Patient responded well with clinical resolution of bronchospasm, clear lung fields,) Tj
T* (and normal SpO2 \(98% on room air\). Afebrile for 48 hours prior to discharge.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (DISCHARGE MEDICATIONS:) Tj
T* (--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T* (1. Tab. Cefuroxime Axetil 500 mg) Tj
T* (   - Dosage: 1 tablet twice daily \(BD\) after food for 5 more days \(Total: 7 days\)) Tj
T* (2. Inhaler Budesonide + Formoterol \(200/6 mcg\)) Tj
T* (   - Route: Metered Dose Inhaler with Spacer) Tj
T* (   - Dosage: 2 puffs twice daily for 30 days, then taper as per clinic review) Tj
T* (3. Tab. Montelukast 10 mg + Levocetirizine 5 mg) Tj
T* (   - Dosage: 1 tablet at bedtime \(OD\) for 14 days) Tj
T* (4. Resume baseline anti-diabetic and anti-hypertensive regimen \(Metformin & Lisinopril\)) Tj
T* () Tj
